  "result_tail": "ose\nThe task didn't specify these, so I picked them; they are documented in the README and covered by tests.\n- **Spaces:** whitespace around parts and around the `-` is ignored, so `\" 1 - 3 , 5 \"` works.\n- **Duplicates:** the result lists each page once, in ascending order, so `\"5,1-3,2-4\"` gives `[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]`.\n- **Backwards ranges:** `\"5-3\"` throws `RangeError` rather than being reversed.\n- **Empty input:** an empty text, or an empty part such as `\"1,\"` or `\"1,,2\"`, throws `RangeError`.\n- **Strict digits:** only plain digits are accepted, so `\"+1\"`, `\"1e1\"` and `\"1.5\"` throw `RangeError`.",
